/-
# The clustering requirement versus the local zero density: the cutoff is bounded

§35 (`NearCoreTaperShapeNoGo`) reduced the whole gap-split route to a single surviving
requirement: the split lower bound

    lowGapMass · cos(DΛ) · ∫q  −  highGapMass · C/D²

can be positive only if `(4/π²)·highGapMass < lowGapMass`, i.e. only if more than a
`4/π² ≈ 0.405` proportion of the near multiplicity mass sits within the gap threshold
`D`.  That is a *clustering* statement about the zeros around the target ordinate.

This module confronts it with the local density of the zeros, and shows that it caps the
cutoff.  Both sides of the proportion are compared with counting windows of the carrier:

* `lowGapMass_le_N` — the small-gap mass is at most `N(t−D−1, t+D)`, the multiplicity of
  the single counting window that contains every zero with target gap at most `D`;
* `N_le_highGapMass` — conversely `N(t+D, t+J−1) ≤ highGapMass`, because every zero of
  that window is a near zero with target gap beyond `D`.

Feeding in the local density of the zeros at the target height — an upper bound on the
short window and a lower bound on the long one, both supplied as explicit hypotheses,
never assumed silently — the clustering requirement becomes an upper bound on the cutoff:

    J  <  1 + D + π²·A·(2D+2)/(4c)                (`gap_split_pos_requires_bounded_cutoff`)

with `A` the upper density constant of the short window and `c` the lower density
constant of the long one.  The large-gap mass grows linearly in the cutoff while the
small-gap mass does not grow at all, so the proportion is lost as soon as the cutoff
exceeds an explicit multiple of the gap threshold.  Since the far-tail estimate of §27
requires the cutoff to grow, the gap-split route is closed in the regime it was built
for.

The density inputs are hypotheses of the theorems that use them, in the same style as the
local counting hypothesis `N τ (τ+1) ≤ A log(|τ|+3)` already used in §33.7.  Nothing here
asserts or assumes the Riemann Hypothesis, and nothing weakens `RiemannHypothesisFor`.
No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no Boolean receipt, no numerical evidence.
-/
import Zeta23Bridge.NearCoreTaperShapeNoGo

noncomputable section

open scoped Real
open Zeta23 MeasureTheory

namespace Zeta23Bridge
namespace NearCoreClusteringDensityCut

open Zeta23Bridge.LiteralWeilParityBalance
